IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwr-common`

-- Fair Work Regulations 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11: fixed term contracts (Part 2-9 Division 5, regs 2.14 and 2.15).
--
-- Seat: the employee on a fixed term contract who wants to know whether the Act's limits on fixed term contracts
-- (s 333E: no more than two years, no more than one extension) protect them, or whether an exception takes the contract
-- outside them (s 333F(1)(e), the high income exception, with reg 2.14; s 333F(1)(i), the prescribed contracts of
-- reg 2.15). A contract inside the limits that breaks them is a contravention the employee can bring a claim about.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 57 (F2026C00996), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F2009L02356.txt.
-- Not deposited, so inputs: the high income threshold figure for the year (reg 2.13 gives the method; see
-- fwr-threshold.l4), whether a body is a philanthropic entity or a recognised sporting organisation, the revenue figures.

§ `reg 2.14 -- the high income threshold for a part-time or part-year contract`

-- Reg 2.14(4): "assume the number of hours that a full-time employee would work is: (a) if an enterprise agreement or a
-- modern award applies to the engaged employee ... the number of hours that a full-time employee is required to work
-- under the enterprise agreement or modern award; or (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply--the number of hours of work of
-- any other full-time employees of the employer employed in the same position (or comparable); or (c) if the number of
-- hours cannot be worked out under paragraph (a) or (b)--38 hours per week."
-- READING (NOTES.md finding 4): (2)(b) needs the full-time hours "in that year", and (c) gives a weekly figure. A year is
-- taken as 52 weeks (1,976 hours). The other reading, 52 1/7 weeks (1,981.43 hours), changes the third decimal place.
-- An input of 0 means "cannot be worked out" under that paragraph.
GIVEN `full-time yearly hours under the agreement or award` IS A NUMBER, `full-time yearly hours of comparable employees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full-time hours for reg 2.14` MEANS
    IF `full-time yearly hours under the agreement or award` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `full-time yearly hours under the agreement or award`
    ELSE IF `full-time yearly hours of comparable employees` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `full-time yearly hours of comparable employees`
         ELSE 38 TIMES 52

-- Reg 2.14(2): "(a) begin with the number of hours that, under the terms of the contract ..., the engaged employee is
-- required to work in that year; (b) divide that number of hours by the number of hours that a full-time employee would
-- work in that year (rounding to 3 decimal places, and rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more); (c)
-- multiply the result of paragraph (b) by the high income threshold, for the financial year in which the contract is
-- entered into". No rounding of the product is prescribed (NOTES.md finding 5), so none is applied.
@export What high income threshold applies to my part-time or part-year fixed term contract (reg 2.14)?
GIVEN `hours my contract requires me to work in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of hours your contract requires you to work in the year it was entered into (parts of an hour allowed)
      `full-time yearly hours under my agreement or award` IS A NUMBER @desc If an enterprise agreement or modern award applied to you when the contract was made, the hours a full-time employee must work under it in that year; otherwise 0
      `full-time yearly hours of comparable employees` IS A NUMBER @desc Otherwise, the yearly hours of your employer's full-time employees in the same or a comparable position; 0 if there are none
      `the high income threshold for the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold (reg 2.13) for the financial year in which the contract was entered into, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my fixed term contract's high income threshold` IS
    (`rounded to 3 decimal places` (`hours my contract requires me to work in the year` DIVIDED BY `the full-time hours`))
        TIMES `the high income threshold for the financial year`
    WHERE
        `the full-time hours` MEANS
            `the full-time hours for reg 2.14` `full-time yearly hours under my agreement or award` `full-time yearly hours of comparable employees`

-- Act s 333F(1)(e): the limits do not apply if "in the year the contract is entered into the amount of the employee's
-- earnings under the contract is above the high income threshold for that year"; s 333F(2): where the employee "is
-- required to work fewer hours than a full-time employee for a year" or "for only part of a year", the threshold is the
-- reg 2.14 amount.
@export Is my fixed term contract outside the fixed term limits because my earnings under it are above the high income threshold (s 333F(1)(e), reg 2.14)?
GIVEN `my earnings under the contract in the year it was made` IS A NUMBER @desc Your earnings under the contract in the year it was entered into, in dollars
      `I work fewer hours than full-time, or only part of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract requires you to work fewer hours than a full-time employee for a year, or for only part of a year
      `hours my contract requires me to work in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of hours your contract requires you to work in that year
      `full-time yearly hours under my agreement or award` IS A NUMBER @desc If an enterprise agreement or modern award applied to you, the yearly hours a full-time employee must work under it; otherwise 0
      `full-time yearly hours of comparable employees` IS A NUMBER @desc Otherwise, the yearly hours of your employer's comparable full-time employees; 0 if there are none
      `the high income threshold for the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold (reg 2.13) for the financial year the contract was entered into, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I above the high income threshold for my fixed term contract` IF
    `my earnings under the contract in the year it was made` GREATER THAN `the threshold that applies`
    WHERE
        `the threshold that applies` MEANS
            IF `I work fewer hours than full-time, or only part of the year`
            THEN `What is my fixed term contract's high income threshold` `hours my contract requires me to work in the year` `full-time yearly hours under my agreement or award` `full-time yearly hours of comparable employees` `the high income threshold for the financial year`
            ELSE `the high income threshold for the financial year`

§ `reg 2.15 -- contracts the fixed term limits do not apply to`

-- Reg 2.15(1)(a) and (2): the kinds of sport work.
DECLARE `Sport role` IS ONE OF
    `an athlete in an organised sport`
    `a coach for such an athlete`
    `another performance support professional for such an athlete`
    `a match official for an organised sport`
    `a performance support professional for a match official`
    `none of these`

-- Reg 2.15(1)(b): the kinds of sport employer.
DECLARE `Sport body` IS ONE OF
    `a recognised National Sporting Organisation`
    `a State or Territory governing body for the sport`
    `the non-metropolitan governing body where they are split`
    `a body running a State or Territory level competition`
    `a member or affiliate of one of those bodies`
    `none of those`

-- Reg 2.15(1): "a contract ... is prescribed if: (a) the employee is engaged under the contract to primarily perform work
-- as" one of the five roles; "and (b) the person is" one of the five bodies; "and (c) the contract is entered into on or
-- after 6 December 2023." An "if" with every head failing answers FALSE.
@export Is my fixed term sport contract outside the fixed term limits (reg 2.15(1))?
GIVEN `my main role under the contract` IS A `Sport role` @desc What you are engaged primarily to do: an athlete, a coach, another performance support professional for an athlete, a match official, a performance support professional for a match official, or none of these
      `my employer` IS A `Sport body` @desc Who you contracted with: a recognised National Sporting Organisation, a State or Territory governing body, a non-metropolitan governing body, a State or Territory competition body, a member or affiliate of one of those, or none of those
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the contract was entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my sport contract outside the limits` IF
        (NOT (`my main role under the contract` EQUALS `none of these`))
    AND (NOT (`my employer` EQUALS `none of those`))
    AND `falls on or before` (Date 6 12 2023) `the day the contract was made`

-- Reg 2.15(3): prescribed if "(a) the employee is engaged ... to perform work that primarily involves direct support of
-- the administration or organisation of a particular international event for a high performance sport; and (b) the
-- international event is not regularly held in Australia; and (c) either: (i) [the person has been] granted ... the
-- right to host the particular international event; or (ii) the person is seeking to be granted the right ...; and (d)
-- the person is: (i) the international organising body ...; or (ii) the Australian organising body for the
-- international event; or (iii) the Australian organising body for the particular international event; and (e) the
-- contract is entered into on or after 6 December 2023." (4): high performance sport is the elite-level part of a sport.
@export Is my fixed term contract supporting an international high performance sport event outside the fixed term limits (reg 2.15(3))?
GIVEN `my work is mainly direct support of running a particular international elite sport event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work primarily involves direct support of the administration or organisation of a particular international event for an elite-level sport
      `the event is not regularly held in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the international event is not regularly held in Australia
      `my employer has, or is seeking, the right to host it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has been granted, or is seeking, the right to host that event
      `my employer is the international or an Australian organising body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is the international organising body, or the Australian organising body, for the event
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the contract was entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my international event contract outside the limits` IF
        `my work is mainly direct support of running a particular international elite sport event`
    AND `the event is not regularly held in Australia`
    AND `my employer has, or is seeking, the right to host it`
    AND `my employer is the international or an Australian organising body`
    AND `falls on or before` (Date 6 12 2023) `the day the contract was made`

-- Regs 2.15(7A), (9A): the relevant entity's revenue "is taken to be" at or over the limit if it is part of a reporting
-- group whose revenue for the most recent financial year was at or over it, "unless the relevant entity provides
-- evidence to the contrary that would satisfy a reasonable person".
GIVEN `the entity's own annual revenue` IS A NUMBER, `its reporting group's revenue` IS A NUMBER,
      `it is in a reporting group` IS A BOOLEAN, `it has evidence to the contrary that would satisfy a reasonable person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revenue is under the limit` IF
    IF `it is in a reporting group` AND `its reporting group's revenue` AT LEAST `the limit` AND (NOT `it has evidence to the contrary that would satisfy a reasonable person`)
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE `the entity's own annual revenue` LESS THAN `the limit`

-- Regs 2.15(7)(i), (9)(j): "the contract is entered into: (i) on or after 1 November 2024; and (ii) before 1 November
-- 2026."
GIVEN `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract falls in the funded-project window` IF
        `falls on or before` (Date 1 11 2024) `the day the contract was made`
    AND `falls before` `the day the contract was made` (Date 1 11 2026)

-- Reg 2.15(7): the charity and not-for-profit exception. "(a) the person is, or enters into the contract on behalf of, a
-- philanthropic entity ...; (aa) the total annual revenue of the relevant entity is less than $10,000,000; (b) the
-- contract relates to a position ... funded in whole or in part by: (i) government funding provided by way of a grant or
-- procurement, other than funding excluded by subregulation (8); or (ii) funding provided by [another] philanthropic
-- entity ...; or (iii) ... a testamentary gift or testamentary contribution ... for a charitable purpose; (c) the work
-- is to be performed for the purposes of a specific program or project to which the funding relates; (d) the period for
-- which the program or project is to be conducted is ... not more than 5 years; (e) the identifiable period ... is
-- substantially the same as the period ... of the program or project; (f) if the employee is already, or has previously
-- been, employed by the person--the employment ... would not result in continuity ... for a period of more than 7
-- years; (g) ... the employee is not covered by either [Higher Education Industry award]; (h) any arrangements for the
-- provision of funding ... take effect on or after 1 November 2024; and (i) the contract is entered into: (i) on or
-- after 1 November 2024; and (ii) before 1 November 2026."
@export Is my fixed term contract with a charity or not-for-profit, on a funded project, outside the fixed term limits (reg 2.15(7))?
GIVEN `my employer is a philanthropic entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is (or contracts for) a philanthropic entity
      `its own total annual revenue` IS A NUMBER @desc That entity's total annual revenue, in dollars
      `it is part of a reporting group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is part of a reporting group under the Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012
      `the reporting group's revenue last financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The reporting group's total annual revenue for the most recent financial year with statements before the contract was made, in dollars (0 if none)
      `it has evidence of lower revenue that would satisfy a reasonable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity has evidence, that would satisfy a reasonable person, that its own revenue is under $10,000,000 despite the group figure
      `my position is funded by qualifying funding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your position is funded by a government grant or procurement (not individual statutory payments or the Commonwealth Home Support Programme), another philanthropic entity, or a testamentary gift for a charitable purpose
      `the work is for the funded program or project` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is for a specific program or project the funding relates to
      `years the program or project runs in all` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years the program or project runs in all, counting any part already run
      `if my contract period is substantially the same as the project's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the period your contract runs for is substantially the same as the (remaining) period of the program or project
      `years of continuous employment with this employer it would make` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have worked for this employer before, how many years of continuous or substantially continuous employment this contract would bring you to (0 if you have not)
      `a Higher Education Industry award covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Higher Education Industry Academic Staff or General Staff Award 2020 covered you when the contract was made
      `the funding arrangements took effect on or after 1 November 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the funding arrangements took effect on or after 1 November 2024
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the contract was entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my charity project contract outside the limits` IF
        `my employer is a philanthropic entity`
    AND `the revenue is under the limit` `its own total annual revenue` `the reporting group's revenue last financial year` `it is part of a reporting group` `it has evidence of lower revenue that would satisfy a reasonable person` 10000000
    AND `my position is funded by qualifying funding`
    AND `the work is for the funded program or project`
    AND `years the program or project runs in all` AT MOST 5
    AND `if my contract period is substantially the same as the project's`
    AND `years of continuous employment with this employer it would make` AT MOST 7
    AND (NOT `a Higher Education Industry award covers me`)
    AND `the funding arrangements took effect on or after 1 November 2024`
    AND `the contract falls in the funded-project window` `the day the contract was made`

-- Reg 2.15(9): the medical or health research exception. As (7), but: (a) the relevant entity is a philanthropic
-- entity, an entity it controls, a body established for a public purpose by or under a law, or an entity such a body
-- controls; (aa) revenue "less than $100,000,000"; (b) government funding (not limited to grants or procurement), another
-- philanthropic entity's funding, or, for a philanthropic entity, funding for its charitable purpose; and (c) "the work
-- primarily involves carrying out medical or health research of any of the following kinds: (i) basic research; (ii)
-- pre-clinical research; (iii) clinical research; (iv) translational research".
@export Is my fixed term contract in medical or health research, on a funded project, outside the fixed term limits (reg 2.15(9))?
GIVEN `my employer is a philanthropic or public-purpose body, or one they control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is (or contracts for) a philanthropic entity, a body established for a public purpose by or under an Australian law, or an entity one of those controls
      `its own total annual revenue` IS A NUMBER @desc That entity's total annual revenue, in dollars
      `it is part of a reporting group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is part of a reporting group under the Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012
      `the reporting group's revenue last financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc The reporting group's total annual revenue for the most recent financial year with statements before the contract was made, in dollars (0 if none)
      `it has evidence of lower revenue that would satisfy a reasonable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity has evidence, that would satisfy a reasonable person, that its own revenue is under $100,000,000 despite the group figure
      `my position is funded by qualifying funding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your position is funded by government funding, another philanthropic entity, or (for a philanthropic employer) funding for its charitable purpose
      `my work is mainly basic, pre-clinical, clinical or translational research` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work primarily involves medical or health research that is basic, pre-clinical, clinical or translational
      `the work is for the funded program or project` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is for a specific program or project the funding relates to
      `years the program or project runs in all` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years the program or project runs in all, counting any part already run
      `if my contract period is substantially the same as the project's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the period your contract runs for is substantially the same as the (remaining) period of the program or project
      `years of continuous employment with this employer it would make` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have worked for this employer before, how many years of continuous or substantially continuous employment this contract would bring you to (0 if you have not)
      `a Higher Education Industry award covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Higher Education Industry Academic Staff or General Staff Award 2020 covered you when the contract was made
      `the funding arrangements took effect on or after 1 November 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the funding arrangements took effect on or after 1 November 2024
      `the day the contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The date the contract was entered into
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my research project contract outside the limits` IF
        `my employer is a philanthropic or public-purpose body, or one they control`
    AND `the revenue is under the limit` `its own total annual revenue` `the reporting group's revenue last financial year` `it is part of a reporting group` `it has evidence of lower revenue that would satisfy a reasonable person` 100000000
    AND `my position is funded by qualifying funding`
    AND `my work is mainly basic, pre-clinical, clinical or translational research`
    AND `the work is for the funded program or project`
    AND `years the program or project runs in all` AT MOST 5
    AND `if my contract period is substantially the same as the project's`
    AND `years of continuous employment with this employer it would make` AT MOST 7
    AND (NOT `a Higher Education Industry award covers me`)
    AND `the funding arrangements took effect on or after 1 November 2024`
    AND `the contract falls in the funded-project window` `the day the contract was made`
